      "description": "jpmorganchase.com publishes no MX records. Its published SPF record is 'v=spf1 a:spf.jpmchase.com ip4:207.162.228.0/24 ip4:207.162.229.0/24 ip4:207.162.225.0/24 ip4:196.37.232.50 ip4:159.53.46.0/24 ip4:159.53.36.0/24 ip4:159.53.110.0/24 ip4:170.148.48.0/24 ip4:159.53.78.0/24 -all'. Its DMARC policy is p=reject, so email is clearly configured here deliberately; the domain appears to send mail without accepting any.",
      "impact": "A sending server has to wait for the lookup to fail and then fall back to the A record before giving up, which delays the bounce and can leave mail queued for days.",
      "remediation": "Publish the null MX record 'MX 0 .' (RFC 7505). It tells senders immediately and unambiguously that this domain accepts no mail, instead of leaving them to infer it.",
